<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 79,864 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 79,864 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 79,864 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 53,536 tonnes on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			14,568	    14,138</p>
<p>    Import cargo			65,296	    39,398</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships are expected to sail and seven to arrive. </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>General cargo	 1,300	  Trima		  due</p>
<p>Steel		   5,760	  Mehmet Basir Agne  10/4</p>
<p>Chemical		3,814	  Owl Trader-2	 11/4</p>
<p>Crude oil	     70,000	 Stavros-1	    12/4</p>
<p>Gas oil		 75,000	 Chesapeak City     13/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
